{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMertckANKQx7YPCmM4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XkAbtTJ2UDB8jpKHWVcCU6","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-85RWx2; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)''','''    # Integer percent: DynamoDB rejects floats, so convert at the boundary.\n    return int(round(100 * (0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score)))''')\ns=s.replace('\"\"\"Shared-tag ratio (Jaccard), blended with shared words of the two bodies.\"\"\"','\"\"\"Shared-tag ratio (Jaccard), blended with shared words of the two bodies.\\n\\n    Returns an int percentage (0-100), never a float.\\n    \"\"\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_second_publish_with_existing_records(self):\n        # The populated-table path computes similarity scores; first-write\n        # tests never reach it.\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"First\", \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"],\n                            \"body\": \"Two crontabs both had the line.\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"Second\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"],\n                                     \"body\": \"A crontab ran twice.\"})\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n        self.assertEqual(len(stored[\"similar\"]), 1)\n        score = stored[\"similar\"][0][\"score\"]\n        self.assertIsInstance(score, int)\n        self.assertTrue(0 <= score <= 100)\n\n    def test_handler_twice_returns_201(self):\n        import json\n        table = FakeTable()\n        for slug in (\"story-one\", \"story-two\"):\n            body = json.dumps({\"slug\": slug, \"title\": \"T\", \"tags\": [\"a\"], \"body\": \"some body text\"})\n            self.assertEqual(app.handler({\"body\": body}, table)[\"statusCode\"], 201)\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests 2>&1 | tail -5\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` in `src/app.py` returned a Python float (`round(0.7*tag + 0.3*word, 4)`).\n`publish()` stores the top-3 matches as `item[\"similar\"]`, each with that float `score`.\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`).\nOn the first publish the table is empty, so `related()` returns `[]`: no scores, no floats, no error.\nFrom the second publish on, scores exist and `put_item` fails (see `logs/error.log`). The bug only exists once there is data.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `similarity()` now returns an integer percentage (0–100), so nothing float-valued reaches `put_item`.\n- Tests: `test_second_publish_with_existing_records` and `test_handler_twice_returns_201` seed a record and then write a second one. That runs the populated-table path, and the fake table rejects floats the way real DynamoDB does. They fail on the old code and pass now.\n\n**Prevention:** every write-path test must seed the table first. The empty-table path happens once in production. Convert computed values (divisions, `round()`) to int or `Decimal` where they enter the item.\n\nNot verified against a real table (no deploy allowed here). Only the fake table was used.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2078,"cache_read_input_tokens":21973,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2078},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10de6410-9010-4453-b1f4-e29fbe0f673e","uuid":"d5e44de6-