{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMg7UFVp8RQXQ8Hm1ug","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish returned 500 because `similarity()` in `src/app.py` returned a float, and boto3 refuses to store floats in DynamoDB. I fixed it and wrote the cause and fix in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `publish()` saves the top 3 related stories with a `score` for each, and that score was `round(0.7*tag + 0.3*word, 4)`, a float. On the first publish the table is empty, so there are no related stories, no scores and no floats. From the second publish on there are scores, and `put_item` raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`.\n\n**Fix:** `similarity()` now returns an integer percentage from 0 to 100.\n\n**Prevention:** I added two tests that seed one story and then publish a second:\n- `test_second_publish_with_existing_records` calls `publish()` directly and checks the score is an int between 0 and 100.\n- `test_handler_twice_returns_201` publishes twice through `handler()` and expects 201 both times.\n\nThe fake table in `tests/fake_dynamo.py` rejects floats the way real DynamoDB does. With the `src/app.py` change stashed, the two new tests fail (one failure, one error). With the fix, all three tests pass.\n\nI only ran this against the fake table, because deploying wasn't allowed here. I didn't publish twice against a real table."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1418,"cache_read_input_tokens":25483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1418},"output_tokens":445,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10de6410-9010-4453-b1f4-e29fbe0f673e","uuid":"b49a9c20-37cf-4e76-8918-5df57480dbaf","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23: